      "writtenOn": "2026-03-24T15:32:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this `order \u0026\u0026` check is redundant with the `order \u003e max_order_direct_reclaim` also included here, and can be removed.\n\nBoth `order` and `max_order_direct_reclaim` are unsigned, so `order` must be `\u003e 0` for `order \u003e max_order_direct_reclaim` to be true.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 121,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 121,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "b291d564905bad43d53912e8617af192fdbcd993",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d3bc5afc_ae07e72b",
        "filename": "drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_pool.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 121,
      "author": {
        "id": 2046240
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-24T16:52:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As presently written, it is equivalent to:\n```\nif ((order \u0026\u0026 !may_direct_reclaim) || (order \u0026\u0026 order \u003e max_order_direct_reclaim))\n```\n\nYou are right that the second term can be simplified (since unsigned) leaving us with:\n```\nif ((order \u0026\u0026 !may_direct_reclaim) || (order \u003e max_order_direct_reclaim))\n```\n\nBut the first term cannot be simplified, otherwise we\u0027d cease from ensuring direct-reclaim is always used for order-0 allocations (which we need to avoid failed allocs when system-wide mem pressure is high).\n\nI prefer the current writing because it makes the order-0 case clear. \nHow about you?",
      "parentUuid": "28bffa51_927f036c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 121,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 121,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "b291d564905bad43d53912e8617af192fdbcd993",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25316cff_40c0acb8",
